    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Liability:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The bill of lading specifies the transportation company's liability in case of any damage or loss during the transportation process.</p>
  </div>
</div>

	<p>To ensure complete protection for your bike during transportation, you should opt for 100% declared-value marine transit insurance. This insurance policy covers any loss or damage to your motorcycle during transit.</p>
	<p>The marine transit insurance covers the bike's declared value, ensuring that you receive compensation in case of any unfortunate incident during transportation. It is recommended to choose a reputable insurance provider for this service.</p>

	<p>Before the bike is picked up for transportation, a vehicle inspection report is essential. This report verifies the bike's current condition and helps in documenting any pre-existing damages.</p>
	<p>During the inspection, the transportation company's representative will carefully inspect the bike and document any existing damages or issues. This report ensures that any new damages during transportation can be attributed to the transit process, rather than pre-existing conditions.</p>

	<p>To ensure a smooth transportation process, it is important to provide accurate and detailed information about your motorcycle.</p></div>
